ental-tribune.com/dti/0001/b85466cb/cmVzaXplLWNyb3Aodz00MDtoPTQwKTpzaGFycGVuKGxldmVsPTApOm91dHB1dChmb3JtYXQ9Z2lmKQ/wp-content/themes/dt/images/company-photo.gif 40w, https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/aec8dcf5/cmVzaXplLWNyb3Aodz02MDtoPTYwKTpzaGFycGVuKGxldmVsPTApOm91dHB1dChmb3JtYXQ9Z2lmKQ/wp-content/themes/dt/images/company-photo.gif 60w, https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/f0d94554/cmVzaXplLWNyb3Aodz0xMjA7aD0xMjApOnNoYXJwZW4obGV2ZWw9MCk6b3V0cHV0KGZvcm1hdD1naWYp/wp-content/themes/dt/images/company-photo.gif 120w, https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/39be7c2e/cmVzaXplLWNyb3Aodz0xNjA7aD0xNjApOnNoYXJwZW4obGV2ZWw9MCk6b3V0cHV0KGZvcm1hdD1naWYp/wp-content/themes/dt/images/company-photo.gif 160w\" type=\"image/gif\"><img src=\"https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/1fc229b3/cmVzaXplLWNyb3Aodz04MDtoPTgwKTpzaGFycGVuKGxldmVsPTApOm91dHB1dChmb3JtYXQ9Z2lmKQ/wp-content/themes/dt/images/company-photo.gif\" alt=\"SprintRay\" loading=\"lazy\">\n\t</picture> <p>SprintRay</p> <p>Mon. 26. October 2026</p> share save <h2><p>WEITERSTADT, Germany: SprintRay, a dental technology company, recently introduced its expanded digital dentistry platform at 3DNext 2026 in Miami Beach in Florida in the US. Its key elements include the Foundation wireless intra-oral scanner and ScanOS, integrated scanning software, as well as the Nano Series compact chairside production system. SprintRay also announced a new restorative resin developed with GC Corp. Together, these developments extend SprintRay’s connected workflow, covering scanning and design to printing and post-processing.</p>\n</h2> <p>“For years, we connected scanning and printing through third-party integrations, but the experience still required practices to move between systems,” said Dr Amir Mansouri, co-founder and CEO of SprintRay. “ScanOS makes scanning a native part of the SprintRay workflow, and Foundation is the first intra-oral scanner built for it. With the Nano Series, we have designed the print, wash and cure experience around the way chairside dentistry actually works.”</p>\n<h2>Foundation and ScanOS: Scanning built into the workflow</h2>\n<p>Foundation is a full-colour intra-oral scanner built for ScanOS, which is integrated into SprintRay’s cloud dashboard. Foundation brings scanning into the same account and interface used for design and production, helping practices to move from digital capture to a finished case without a separate file export or upload step after scanning.</p>\n<p>The “Scan” tab sits alongside the SprintRay dashboard’s design and production tools. When scanning is complete, files are available in the cloud for the next workflow step.</p>\n<p>Foundation will initially launch in the US, and the first shipments are expected in November. In Europe, the Middle East and Africa, Foundation is expected to become available in the first quarter of 2027.</p><picture><source srcset=\"https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/07cff571/cmVzaXplLWNyb3Aodz0yNDA7aD0xMzUpOnNoYXJwZW4obGV2ZWw9MCk6b3V0cHV0KGZvcm1hdD13ZWJwKQ/up/dt/2026/10/SprintRay-moves-beyond-3D-printing-with-expanded-digital-dentistry-platform-1.jpg 240w, https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/3bb4cc20/cmVzaXplLWNyb3Aodz0xMjA7aD02OCk6c2hhcnBlbihsZXZlbD0wKTpvdXRwdXQoZm9ybWF0PXdlYnAp/up/dt/2026/10/SprintRay-moves-beyond-3D-printing-with-expanded-digital-dentistry-platform-1.jpg 120w, https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/2ee11256/cmVzaXplLWNyb3Aodz0xODA7aD0xMDIpOnNoYXJwZW4obGV2ZWw9MCk6b3V0cHV0KGZvcm1hdD13ZWJwKQ/up/dt/2026/10/SprintRay-moves-beyond-3D-printing-with-expanded-digital-dentistry-platform-1.jpg 180w, https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/9f5c3877/cmVzaXplLWNyb3Aodz0zNjA7aD0yMDMpOnNoYXJwZW4obGV2ZWw9MCk6b3V0cHV0KGZvcm1hdD13ZWJwKQ/up/dt/2026/10/SprintRay-moves-beyond-3D-printing-with-expanded-digital-dentistry-platform-1.jpg 360w, https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/5e05db4e/cmVzaXplLWNyb3Aodz00ODA7aD0yNzApOnNoYXJwZW4obGV2ZWw9MCk6b3V0cHV0KGZvcm1hdD13ZWJwKQ/up/dt/2026/10/SprintRay-moves-beyond-3D-